% Respect the format.


% Format for DV
% ID   MOD   IDSUBDV   


% Format for SUBDV
% ID TAG  IDTAG  SUBTAG  VAL 

% Format for SUBRESP
% ID TAG  IDTAG  SUBTAG 

% Format for RESP
% ID MOD    AGGREG/TYPE    IDSUBRESPGROUP(if MOD is MULT)    %EXTRAVALS (if AGGREG is KS) 



%========   DVS ================

% ID   MOD   IDSUBDV   Value

% --- ID
%  id of the DV
% --- MOD
% Could be SING / MULT   
% --- IDSUBDV
% If MOD is SING, it si the ID of the subdv. If MOD=MULTI, then is the ID of the group of subdvs


% Example
$INIDV
1     SING   1      0.00635
2     SING   2     0.005334
3     SING   3     0.004572
4     SING   4     0.003302
5     SING   5      0.00254
6     SING   6     0.001651
7     SING   7      0.01905
8     SING   8      0.01524
9     SING   9       0.0127
10    SING  10     0.009525
11    SING  11      0.00508
12    SING  12      0.00254
$ENDDV




$INISUBDV
1     PROP   1  THICKNESS
2     PROP   2  THICKNESS
3     PROP   3  THICKNESS
4     PROP   4  THICKNESS
5     PROP   5  THICKNESS
6     PROP   6  THICKNESS
7     PROP   7  THICKNESS
8     PROP   8  THICKNESS
9     PROP   9  THICKNESS
10    PROP  10  THICKNESS
11    PROP  11  THICKNESS
12    PROP  12  THICKNESS
$ENDSUBDV




$INISUBRESP
1  STRESS     1  VM   CENTROID   TOP                      
$ENDSUBRESP


$INIRESP
1     MULT      1   KS     50.0     
$ENDRESP



